module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.green_reported_over_a_population_the_instrument_does_not_own

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data green_reported_over_a_population_the_instrument_does_not_own: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "green_reported_over_a_population_the_instrument_does_not_own" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an instrument reports GREEN over a population it does not own, so a fact can be filed in an authority, absent from the projection readers are pointed at, and nothing refuses** (INVALID STATE: two actuators split one generated-artifact population, and the one lanes habitually run denominates only its own half. ",

    "`claim_executor --required-regen` reports `first_generation_equal=true planned=155 executed=155 adjudicated=155` while `docs/design-failure-modes.md` is STALE, because the ledger projections are produced by a different actuator entirely -- `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/gunbc/instruments/generated_artifact_gate.dag --function main_wet`. ",

    "HARM: a lane files a row in `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode`, runs the regen, sees 155/155/155, and stops -- having shipped a row that exists in the authority and nowhere a reader can see it, since DESIGN.md points readers at the projection and not at the .dag. ",

    "The green is not merely uninformative about the projection; it is READ as covering it, because the instrument's name and its round numbers make no distinction between the population it adjudicated and the population it was asked about. ",

    "SPECIMEN, and it is the row filed beside this one: `absence_classifier_default_bucket` was authored into the authority, `--required-regen` returned first_generation_equal=true, and the projection still did not contain it. ",

    "The gap was found by GREPPING THE PROJECTION for the row just filed, which is not a step any gate performs. ",

    "THE TWO NEIGHBOURS THIS IS NOT, cited so the family is readable and this row is not consolidated into either. ",

    "[[incidental_denominator_as_wall]] is THE SAME DENOMINATOR SHAPE WITH THE OPPOSITE SIGN: there, `is_compared_generated_basename` -- whose job is to denominate the DRIFT COMPARISON -- accidentally CREATED safety by never handing an installer a dangerous input, so nothing is wrong today and the harm is that the protection is uncredited and dissolves silently when the upstream question changes. ",

    "Here the same accident runs the other way: a denominator written for one question accidentally DESTROYS COVERAGE while continuing to report green, and something IS wrong today. ",

    "Uncredited protection versus credited assurance that is not there. ",

    "[[authority_merges_unprotected_while_its_projection_is_guarded]] is a MERGE-TIME protection asymmetry over the same file pair -- projection driver-bound, hand-authored authority matching no merge attribute -- repaired by binding the driver to the authority path. ",

    "This row is REGEN-TIME and is reachable with no merge in sight. ",

    "(Two notes worth keeping. ",

    "That merge row landed in the very merge that conflicted the branch filing this one, and it had already measured the 16,792-character line 144 that made the conflict hazardous -- the hazard was filed by another lane before this one hit it. ",

    "And it has since been observed firing in production on a SIBLING lane's head: `git merge-tree --write-tree` returned rc=1 with BOTH projections refusing while `gh pr view` reported mergeable=MERGEABLE on that same commit, observed simultaneously -- a cleaner specimen of that row than the one it was filed with, and a second instrument disagreeing with a green.) A SECOND SPECIMEN, RECORDED BECAUSE THE AUTHOR OF THIS ROW COMMITTED THE SAME SHAPE WITHIN THE HOUR OF FILING IT, IN THE OPPOSITE DIRECTION: asked whether CI would ever run on a merge-conflicted head, they polled one branch once a minute for six minutes, observed no run, and reported that GitHub does not create runs for a head it cannot merge -- a NEVER claimed from an instrument whose denominator was one branch and six minutes. ",

    "The control was one command away and refuted it: three other DIRTY pull requests in the same repository carried six and seven check-runs each, while the two heads at zero were simply the two most recently pushed, one dirty and one clean, under a backlog of sixty-two unfinished runs. ",

    "Recency separated the population perfectly and dirtiness did not separate it at all. ",

    "The general form is this row's own, with the sign flipped: there an instrument's GREEN was read as covering a population it never enumerated; here an instrument's SILENCE was. ",

    "A transient state proves nothing about membership without duration or a control already sitting in the state being called impossible -- and DESIGN section 5 names the tell in advance, since NEVER is the word that lets a ratchet pass as a wall. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when an instrument reports a clean round count, ask WHICH ARTIFACTS ITS DENOMINATOR ENUMERATES and whether the artifact you changed is among them -- a per-artifact count is evidence about the artifacts counted and says nothing whatever about the ones the actuator does not own, while reading exactly like whole-population coverage. ",

    "The tell is two actuators over one declared population with no join between their denominators. ",

    "THE FORMER NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER FIRED ON 2026-09-04, AND IS RETIRED BY ITS TRIGGER AND BY NOTHING ELSE. gunbc#10455 deleted RegenPhase from both gunbc.required_ci_phase_roster RequiredCiPhase and its host realization, moved its stage0-mirror adjudicator under the surviving GeneratedArtifactPhase beside the registry-projection adjudicator, runs the second population even when the first refuses, and emits one terminal OK or FAIL naming both populations. A stale projection or drifted mirror now refuses from the SAME phase and neither half can lend its green to the other. ",

    "RUNG: MITIGATABLE, WHICH IS THE MINIMUM ACROSS THIS CLASS'S IN-SCOPE PATHS AND NOT THE STRONGER ARM'S. Two paths are in scope and they sit at different rungs. THE GENERATED-ARTIFACT PATH IS MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE, and the paragraph below states why. THE LOCAL PRE-PUSH PATH IS MITIGATABLE: nothing computes whether a local instrument's population contains a changed path, so a green from a run that never opened the file is still readable as coverage, and the 2026-09-08 specimen below was caught only because the required lane refused after the push. DESIGN section 4b(1) makes the reported rung the minimum across in-scope paths, so this row reports MITIGATABLE -- and it must, because scoping the lower rung to `this specimen` while leaving the class line at the stronger arm would be the same inflation this row's mirror-arm paragraph already refuses, committed in the row whose whole subject is an instrument read as covering what it does not. THE GENERATED-ARTIFACT PATH, at mechanically preventable: the invalid source shape remains writable: the bootstrap host can still omit one component call or reintroduce an independently-green phase, and safety depends on the composite phase executing and its permanent controls staying enrolled. It is therefore not structural guarantee or impossibility. ",

    "EXECUTED EVIDENCE FOR THE CLIMB. The permanent floor-discovered controls refuse both asymmetric states -- registry green with a drifted stage0 mirror, and mirrors green with a stale registry projection -- while an all-clean positive control accepts, excluding a compositor that merely refuses everything. On gunbc#10455's required CI execution the announced phase roster omitted regen and the surviving phase reported `generated-artifact OK populations=registry-projections,stage0-mirrors`; independently, the authoring run observed stage0-mirrors 156/156 clean, continued into a typed registry MemoryStallRefusedPageThrash instead of short-circuiting, and emitted the single terminal composite FAIL naming both populations. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, from mechanically preventable to structurally guaranteed: required-run dispatch and heal-before-push consume an exhaustive adjudicator DERIVED from every arm of gunbc.required_ci_phase_roster DeclaredGeneratedArtifactPopulation, such that adding an arm without an adjudicator is a compile refusal and neither consumer can construct Accepted until every arm returns clean. This is the missing construction; a test that the current two calls remain present would only add another mechanical wall.)",
    "THREE SPECIMENS FROM THE 2026-09-04 OUTAGE, filed after the climb rather than before it, because they are the record of what the lower rung COST and a class that climbs with no account of that will not be believed the next time it is invoked. (i) THE AUTOMATED-ACTOR FORM, which is strictly worse than the unmeasured half this row was founded on: `#10402` landed an `src/v1/04_infer.dag` change without regenerating `src/v1/stage0/src/v1_compiler_infer.rs`, and on every affected pull request `heal-generated-artifacts` RAN, SUCCEEDED and PUSHED A COMMIT of `1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)` -- that one file being the projection. The drifted mirror was never in heal's population, so heal did not merely fail to notice it: it MANUFACTURED A FRESH GREEN HEAD OVER A TREE ANOTHER REQUIRED PHASE WAS REFUSING, on every affected branch, indefinitely. `wait for the heal push` was therefore not a terminating strategy, and four lanes inherited the same red at once while both gates reported truthfully about their own halves. ",

    "(ii) THE CI-EXECUTED TWO-CELL TABLE, which the founding receipt could not offer because it had local counts only: the same two jobs compared across two runs, main against a branch carrying the regeneration. `required-witnesses-build` main FAILURE with `FAILED PHASE regen`, branch SUCCESS with no such line; `required-witnesses-floor` FAILURE on both with a byte-identical message. Carrying the regeneration flips the owning job on the real acceptance path, and the second red is orthogonal -- a fact establishable only from the one tree in the fleet that had repaired the first half. ",

    "(iii) THE POSITIVE HALF, and the first independent confirmation that resolving the authority and letting heal regenerate is CORRECT rather than merely convenient: an independent local derive of the projection from the merged authorities produced bytes IDENTICAL to heal's, while the mirror hashes differed in the same measurement. Two producers agreeing exactly on the population they share and only one ranging over the population they do not is this row's tell demonstrated in both directions at once. `#10357` later landed two of those regenerated mirrors byte-identical to an independently produced candidate, which is a second confirmation of the same shape. ",

    "THE CLIMB IS COMPLETE IN SCOPE AND NOT IN DENOMINATOR, and this row must say so or it becomes the very thing it names. The unified phase adjudicates both declared populations, but the two arms are not the same instrument and only one of them counts: `population=registry-projections rostered=39 adjudicated=39 matches=38 drifted=1 absent=0 unadjudicated=0` against `population=stage0-mirrors first_generation_equal=true` and NO numeric field whatever. The projection arm is an identity join carrying a conservation assert; the mirror arm is a byte fixed-point over a candidate. So an unregistered MIRROR is still invisible -- a check whose population IS the roster cannot see an artifact missing from the roster -- and `one adjudication over the whole declared population` is true of the phase's SCOPE while remaining false of its DENOMINATOR. ",

    "SECOND NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, at the mirror arm's own subject grain and distinct from the structural trigger above: a ROSTERED DENOMINATOR for `population=stage0-mirrors`, reporting rostered/adjudicated/unadjudicated with the same conservation the projection arm already carries, sufficient that a stage0 mirror absent from the roster is a REFUSAL rather than an artifact nobody counted. Until that exists the mirror path is weaker than the projection path, and DESIGN 4b(1) makes this row's rung the MINIMUM across its in-scope paths rather than the stronger arm's -- so citing the registry arm's conservation as though it covered the mirrors would be exactly the inflation this class is about.)",

    "A SECOND SPECIMEN, IN A DIFFERENT INSTRUMENT PAIR, FILED AND NOT REPAIRED (2026-09-08) -- and it folds here rather than minting a row because the CAUSE is this row's cause exactly: an instrument reports green over a population that does not contain the subject it is being read as covering. What differs is only which population, and that difference is not a different mechanism. ",

    "THE SUBJECT: an edit to `gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing`, a `.dag` authority module. The edit carried a PARSE ERROR -- in `.dag` a data expression may not begin on the line after `=`, and the constructor had been broken onto the following line. TWO LOCAL INSTRUMENTS WERE RUN ON THE BROKEN FORM AND BOTH RETURNED GREEN: `claim_executor --required-floor` reported `verdict=FloorClean` with `planned=executed=terminal` and `claims_failed=0`, and the docs projection regen (`gunbc run ... docs_projection_gate --function regen`) wrote its outputs and exited zero. The author reported FloorClean on the strength of those two readings. The required lane then refused on the pushed head at `phase=parse`, naming the file and the exact error `expected expression, found Newline`. THE PHASE IS THE LOAD-BEARING PART: the required run's PARSE SWEEP is its own phase over `DAG_PARSE_SWEEP_ROOTS` -- `src/v1`, `dag`, `src/v2` -- independent of the floor beneath it. ",

    "WHY BOTH GREENS WERE VACUOUS, VERIFIED RATHER THAN INFERRED, and this is the part that makes it this class and not carelessness: NEITHER INSTRUMENT PARSES THAT FILE AT ALL. No module in the corpus imports `gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing` -- checked directly, there is no import statement naming it anywhere -- so no witness reaches it BY IMPORT; and it is not itself a witness module, so no witness carries it as a ROOT either. BOTH CONJUNCTS, DERIVED AGAINST THE ROOT SET RATHER THAN ASSERTED -- which is what this row's own closing paragraph demands of every visibility claim in it, this one included. The floor, whose population is planned witness claims, therefore never reaches it. The projection regen's population is the ledger authorities it renders, which does not include this module either. The required lane reaches it because its PARSE PHASE ranges over ALL SOURCES UNDER THE SWEEP ROOTS, which is a third population owned by neither local instrument. Three instruments, three populations, and the subject was in exactly one of them. ",

    "WHICH BRANCH THIS IS, MEASURED BEFORE FILING, because two different faults produce the same green and only one of them is this class. EITHER the file was in the instrument's planned population and was parsed and TOLERATED -- right denominator, insufficient predicate, which would be a different class -- OR it was never in the population at all. IT IS THE SECOND, and the measurement is one grep: NO IMPORT STATEMENT ANYWHERE IN THE CORPUS NAMES `gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing`. The one witness that appears to reach it, `test.claim.documentary_refs_witness`, imports `gunbc.documentary_refs` and consumes a `DeclarationRef` carrying the module PATH AS A STRING -- a reference, not an import -- so the module enters no parse closure. The parser was never tolerant; it was never asked. ",

    "AND THE UNIMPORTED STATE IS SPECIFIC TO THIS MODULE RATHER THAN A PROPERTY OF THE DIRECTORY, which is what turns one observation into a finding. Census over every module in `dag/gunbc/v1/`, counting importers by their real module paths -- these are `gunbc.<name>` with NO `v1` path segment, and a census keyed on the DIRECTORY spelling matches nothing and manufactures ten false positives: `v1_maintenance_standing` is THE ONLY ONE WITH ZERO IMPORTERS. Every sibling is imported, with non-zero importer counts throughout, which is the discriminating control -- a census that found zero everywhere would be measuring its own key rather than the corpus. The counts themselves are deliberately not transcribed: re-derive them with the census rather than reading a number that rots on the next import (DESIGN section 6). So the specimen is not `an authority module happens to be unimported`; it is that the one module in that directory GOVERNING EVERY v1 ADMISSION is also the one nothing imports, against a ten-sibling control establishing that the pattern is not directory-wide. The producer is the census itself -- for each module in that directory, count files whose import statements name it -- and the positive control that makes it trustworthy is that the control modules come back NON-ZERO. ",

    "THREE NEIGHBOURS DISPOSED OF EXPLICITLY, because all three are about a denominator and a reader must be able to tell which one owns this. [[required_lane_green_over_a_population_it_never_offered]] is the closest and is still not it: its population is DECLARED CLAIMS that preparation did not offer this run -- the floor PRINTS them, under `outside this run's universe ... declared, but preparation never offered them` -- so its subject is a member of the gate's own declared population, merely absent from one run, and its repair is to offer the claim. This subject carries no claim at all, appears in no exclusion list, and there is nothing to offer; it is a source file that NEITHER LOCAL INSTRUMENT'S population contains -- the floor's roots being planned witness claims and the regen's the ledger authorities it renders -- WHILE THE REQUIRED LANE'S PARSE PHASE, RANGING OVER ALL SOURCES UNDER THE SWEEP ROOTS, DOES CONTAIN IT, which is why that lane refused it by name and why this row has a specimen at all. An earlier draft of this sentence said `no instrument's population contains it` and thereby denied, two sentences before restating it, the founding observation of the whole receipt. [[instrument_answers_outside_its_domain]] requires the instrument to ANSWER about the subject and answer wrongly, its direction set by which way the domain gap points; here neither instrument answered about the subject in any direction -- the greens were true statements about other populations. [[check_subject_shape_cannot_represent_the_state_the_check_detects]] does not fire either: the invalid state was perfectly representable and WAS represented, and the required lane refused it by name. Nothing about the subject's shape hid it. ",

    "THE RECOGNITION RULE THIS SPECIMEN ADDS, and it is sharper than `check what the instrument denominates` because it is answerable before running anything: ASK WHETHER THE INSTRUMENT WOULD EVEN READ THE BYTES YOU CHANGED. A green from a run that never opened the file is not weak evidence, it is no evidence, and it is worse than no check because its green gets spent. For a `.dag` authority module the mechanical test is two questions, and the first is the one an import grep alone will miss: IS THE MODULE A ROOT OF THAT INSTRUMENT, and if not, IS IT REACHABLE BY IMPORTS FROM ONE OF ITS ROOTS. Only when both answers are no can the instrument refuse nothing in it. ",

    "THE MECHANICAL CONDITION IS TWO CONJUNCTS -- THE SUBJECT IS NOT A ROOT OF THAT INSTRUMENT, AND NO ROOT REACHES IT THROUGH IMPORTS -- and it is stated first here because two earlier drafts led with the import count alone and a reader who carries away a topic sentence would have carried away the refuted form. VISIBILITY IS A RELATION BETWEEN A MODULE AND ONE INSTRUMENT, decided by that instrument's own root set, so both conjuncts are asked PER INSTRUMENT and never once for all of them. The import count is the second conjunct: for a given instrument that does not carry the subject as a root, a module nothing imports is a module that instrument cannot read, so `no fold consumes it` and `no gate of that instrument can refuse it` are the same statement seen from two directions. Zero importers alone is NOT sufficient, and the refutation is live in this tree and is the very module this row already cites: `test.claim.documentary_refs_witness` has ZERO importers -- nothing in `dag` or `src/v2` imports it -- and the floor parses it on every run, because a witness module is a ROOT of the floor closure rather than a leaf reached from one. So the row contains its own counterexample to the one-conjunct form, which is why the narrowing is recorded as a MEASURED correction and not a logical caveat. ",

    "BOTH CONJUNCTS ARE ESTABLISHED FOR THIS SPECIMEN, which is why the incident stands unweakened by the narrowing. `gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing` is not a root of the floor -- the floor's roots are planned witness claims -- and not a root of the docs projection regen, whose roots are the ledger authorities it renders; and no root reaches it by import, since nothing imports it at all. The correction is to the general sentence, not to the measurement. ",

    "THE 3c CONSUMPTION ANSWER IS A CORRELATE AND NOT A CAUSE, and the earlier draft asserted the converse as a law: `any carrier whose declared consumption route is human review is, for exactly that reason, invisible to every instrument whose population is derived from the import graph`. THAT IS FALSE. Consumption route and import count are independent facts: a module may answer section 3c with `consumed by review diligence, not by any gate` and still be imported by ten other modules -- and being imported buys VISIBILITY-AS-POSSIBILITY and nothing stronger, since a given instrument still needs a root that reaches one of those importers. The docs projection regen parses none of the v1 modules however heavily they are imported, because its roots are the ledger authorities it renders. The ten imported siblings measured above are exactly the population whose consumption answers this row never measured and therefore has no basis to generalise over. The review answer made the blindness UNSURPRISING here; it did not cause it. What made it PREDICTABLE at authoring time is the import census, which is the thing to run. ",

    "AND THE ERROR IS THE ONE THIS ROW ALREADY REFUSES ONE PARAGRAPH UP, which is why it is recorded rather than quietly corrected: a shared property between two cases was promoted to an identity law and made to do the work the measured predicate should do. The fold argument on [[absence_classifier_default_bucket]] deletes a universal for precisely that reason and grounds on the shared cause instead. Committing the same move in the adjacent paragraph is worth this sentence, and not a second class. ",

    "AND THE PROPAGATION IS THE PART WORTH GENERALISING, because it is what made one wrong sentence cost four corrections in a day: A CORRECTED CLAIM PROPAGATES SLOWER THAN THE CLAIM ITSELF. The over-broad form had already been copied into this paragraph's own topic sentence and into a second pull request's body before the repair landed, so fixing the site a reviewer named left two live copies standing -- each of them load-bearing, and one of them two sentences from its own retraction. THE CENSUS IS THEREFORE NOT `DID I FIX THE FLAGGED LINE` BUT `WHERE ELSE HAVE I ALREADY SAID THIS`, and its domain is every surface the claim reached -- pull request bodies and commit messages included -- not just the diff under review. A claim's blast radius is where it was REPEATED, and repetition leaves no diff. ",

    "AND THE UNDERLYING HABIT IS SYMMETRIC, WHICH IS THE TRANSFERABLE FORM AND IS NOT WHAT THE FIRST TWO CORRECTIONS SUGGESTED. This row made the same error in BOTH DIRECTIONS: it over-claimed INVISIBILITY (zero importers, therefore invisible to every closure-driven instrument) and then, IN THE PARAGRAPH REPAIRING THAT, over-claimed VISIBILITY (many importers, therefore parsed by every closure-driven instrument). Reading the first corrections as `keep remembering the root conjunct` would have predicted neither the second direction nor the next one. THE HABIT IS ASSERTING A UNIVERSAL OVER INSTRUMENTS WHERE THE FACT IS PER-INSTRUMENT: visibility is a relation between a module and ONE instrument, decided by that instrument's own root set, so NO PROPERTY OF THE MODULE ALONE -- import count included -- settles it for all of them. THE RESULTING CHECK IS A SMELL TEST AND NOT A CENSUS, AND THIS ROW MUST SAY SO RATHER THAN SHIP IT AS SUFFICIENT. The cheap form -- grep for sentences quantifying over `every instrument` or `no instrument`, in either direction, and re-derive each -- is correct in principle and UNDER-INCLUSIVE IN PRACTICE, because a universal over instruments can be carried by a possessive, a plural, a `none of`, an `any`, or by a bare generic noun with no quantifier word at all. IT IS NOT A HYPOTHETICAL LIMIT: run on this row, that grep missed a fourth site reading `no instrument's population contains it` -- a possessive -- which was not merely over-broad but an outright SELF-CONTRADICTION, denying two sentences before its own restatement that the required lane's parse-sweep population contained the file and refused it. SO THE CHECK WRITTEN TO CLOSE THIS CLASS DID NOT CLOSE IT, in a row about instruments read as covering what they do not, which makes the under-inclusive grep a defect of exactly the kind this row names, committed inside its own repair. THE REAL CHECK IS THE EXPENSIVE ONE AND THERE IS NO CHEAP SUBSTITUTE: re-derive each claim about visibility against the named instrument's ROOT SET. The grep is worth running first because it is free, and is worth nothing as evidence that the row is clean. ",

    "TWO MORE INSTANCES, BOTH ABOUT VERIFYING A GENERATED ARTIFACT, BOTH MEASURED ON THIS ROW'S OWN LANDING (2026-09-08), and they are filed here rather than as new rows because the cause is this row's cause with the POPULATION set to `my delta`. FIRST, THE AUTHOR SIDE: `THE INSTRUMENT RAN` AND `THE ARTIFACT CARRIES MY CHANGE` ARE DIFFERENT FACTS. A commit landed carrying BOTH the edited authority and a regenerated projection, and the projection was a faithful rendering of a tree that no longer existed -- the regen had run, a further authority edit followed, and the second regen's output reached the worktree AFTER the commit and sat uncommitted. Nothing local refused: the diffstat shows both files, every check the author ran was green, and the staleness was found only when an unrelated checkout balked on a dirty file. A regeneration is evidence about the state it read, and committing one proves only that SOME state was rendered. ",

    "SECOND, THE REVIEWER SIDE, AND IT IS THE SUBTLER OF THE TWO: A GREP FOR A PHRASE YOU CHOSE IS NOT A CONTENT CHECK, BECAUSE YOU CHOOSE THE PHRASE FROM WHAT YOU ALREADY BELIEVE CHANGED. The reviewer confirming that healed projection grepped it for one corrected phrase, found it, and reported the artifact correct. The phrase was present in the stale projection ALL ALONG; the edit actually missing was a different one, and no choice of search string made before knowing the delta could have found it. The verdict was right by luck, which is the worst way for a check to be right, since luck leaves no signal that the check failed. TWO INSTRUMENTS ARE REQUIRED AND NEITHER SUBSUMES THE OTHER, and an earlier draft of this receipt named only the first AS `THE` SOUND INSTRUMENT -- a singular definite article, which is how a check gets read as sufficient, and which contradicted a distinction its own author had drawn one exchange earlier. FIXED POINT: re-run the generator on the head under test and REQUIRE NO DIFF. PROVES the artifact is what THIS GENERATOR PRODUCES FROM THIS TREE; it carries no chosen phrase so it cannot be steered by the checker's expectations; it catches a stale projection, a partial write and a hand edit, and it is what established the healed projection was the fixed point. MISSES: it is the generator agreeing with ITSELF, so a generator that deterministically omits a sentence reproduces its own output exactly, passes forever, and the authored content never lands. AUTHORED-DELTA ARRIVAL: diff the AUTHORITY between the two commits, extract every sentence it gained, and require each present in the projection. PROVES the content actually written REACHED THE ARTIFACT A READER CONSUMES; catches the silent drop fixed-point cannot see. MISSES: everything outside the delta -- it says nothing about content the commit did not touch, so a projection stale in another region passes it. THERE IS NO `THE` HERE, AND THE SINGULAR IS THE DEFECT: a reader who runs one because a row called it the sound instrument commits this row's own failure, which is why both are named with what they MISS rather than one with its virtues. ",

    "WHY BOTH BELONG TO THIS CLASS AND NOT BESIDE IT: in each, a green was read as covering a population it did not own -- the regen's population was a previous tree, and the grep's population was one phrase rather than the delta -- and in each the reader supplied the coverage the instrument never claimed. ",

    "RUNG FOR THIS SPECIMEN: mitigatable -- the required lane DID refuse, loudly and located, naming the file and the error; what failed is the local pre-push instrument, and the cost was a paid runner cycle plus a green the author reported and then had to withdraw. CEILING: mechanically preventable. Whether an instrument's population contains a given path is decidable from data the run already holds, so a local instrument can report the population it adjudicated and refuse to be read as covering a changed path outside it. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, at capability grain and deliberately NOT `authors should run the right command`: A LOCAL INSTRUMENT REFUSES TO RETURN A VERDICT ABOUT ANY PATH OUTSIDE THE POPULATION IT ADJUDICATED, rather than returning a verdict the reader must join by hand -- sufficient that an author asking a local run whether it covered a given file gets a refusal naming the omission, never a green. An instrument that merely PRINTS its population is insufficient -- it leaves the join to the reader, which is the step that failed here. THE POPULATION IS THE INSTRUMENT'S OWN, NOT THE CHANGED-FILE SET, and this is stated because the nearest wrong spelling is one this row already retracted twice below: what the instrument adjudicates stays whatever it adjudicates -- for the floor, its witness closure; for the sweep, all sources under its roots -- and the changed set is only the QUESTION a reader puts to it. A trigger phrased as `an instrument whose population is the changed-file set` is the retracted claim wearing the new trigger's clothes.

WHAT THIS TRIGGER DELIBERATELY DOES NOT PROMISE, in the words the ceiling makes honest: IT DOES NOT STOP THE DEFECT REACHING A PUSH. IT MAKES THE GREEN UNSPENDABLE. The harm this specimen actually records is not that a parse error reached CI -- the required lane refused it, loudly and located. It is that two local instruments returned green and the author READ THEM AS COVERAGE of a file neither had opened. Refusing the verdict removes exactly that, and nothing else. It is decidable, because population membership is data the run already holds; it needs no hook, no new surface and no ruling; and it retires by its own trigger, because once it lands this specimen is unwritable -- neither instrument could have answered green about that file, since neither would have answered about it at all. AND THE TRIGGER NAMES THE BINDING BECAUSE THE INSTRUMENT ALREADY EXISTS, which an earlier draft of this row got wrong TWICE and which is recorded rather than quietly corrected. That draft demanded `a locally runnable instrument whose population is the CHANGED-FILE SET of the working tree`. BOTH HALVES WERE FALSE. the `v1_src_dag_parse` cargo bin is already exactly such an instrument: it and the required run's parse phase both call `run_dag_parse_sweep` over the shared `DAG_PARSE_SWEEP_ROOTS` roster, so they are ONE WALK OVER ONE SUBJECT and it is not a second authority -- measured on a clean tree in SECONDS RATHER THAN MINUTES -- the figure is deliberately not transcribed, since it moves with the sweep roots and the machine; re-derive it by running the bin -- and measured against this row's own specimen by reintroducing the defect, where it refuses WITH FILE AND LINE, which is better location than the required lane produced. A trigger naming an already-built capability can never be retired by its trigger, so the row would have sat on main claiming a climb was blocked when it was not -- an UNEARNED BLOCKED STATUS, which is rung inflation's mirror and has the same effect: the class never ranks for climbing. AND THE POPULATION WAS MISCHARACTERISED TOO: the operative distinction is not changed-versus-unchanged but ALL SOURCES UNDER THE SWEEP ROOTS versus THE WITNESS CLOSURE. The floor misses this module because the closure excludes it, not because it was unchanged, and the `changed-file` framing was inferred from a diagnostic NAME seen in a log -- `ChangedWitnessObservationFailed`, which belongs to the FLOOR runner and NOT to the parse phase at all -- rather than from what any instrument enumerates. AND THE RETRACTION HAD TO REACH EVERY SENTENCE ASSERTING IT: an earlier head retracted it here while three other paragraphs still asserted it as fact, and a row that retracts in one place and asserts in three has not retracted. AND THE THIRD CORRECTION IS TO THE TRIGGER ITSELF, RECORDED IN FULL BECAUSE THIS ROW'S TRIGGER HAS NOW BEEN WRONG THREE TIMES IN THREE DIFFERENT WAYS -- unbuilt, already-built, and now naming a surface the corpus forbids. The head before this one read WHAT IS ACTUALLY ABSENT IS THE BINDING, and demanded the parse sweep be bound to a gate a developer runs by default, sufficient that a parse error `cannot reach a push locally`. THAT SUFFICIENCY CLAUSE IS UNSATISFIABLE BY ANY LOCAL SURFACE THAT EXISTS, which is what makes it a defect rather than an unbuilt item. Every `.githooks` surface fails three tests at once -- opt-in per clone through the `core.hooksPath` seed, bypassable with `--no-verify`, and absent in container worktrees -- and the 2026-07-25 operator ruling recorded at `gunbc.githooks_pre_push_emit` `pre_push_fmt_only_note` forbids re-heavying that hook in the first place. THE ONE NON-HOOK LOCAL SURFACE THAT PASSES ALL THREE TESTS IS `src/v1/stage0/build.rs`, AND IT CANNOT HOST THE CHECK EITHER: a build script runs BEFORE the crate whose binary it would need, which is a cycle and not a policy objection. So NONE is derived here rather than surveyed, and the conclusion is that the only enforcing surface is the required lane, which is not local. A TRIGGER WHOSE CONSEQUENCE NO SURFACE CAN PRODUCE is retired by nothing, exactly as DESIGN section 4b(3) says of a trigger naming less than the capability it restores -- the failure is the same shape from the opposite side, promising MORE than any capability can deliver rather than less. The trigger above therefore drops enforcement entirely and buys the one thing that is reachable. The absent binding is still recorded, as a fact and not as an obligation: the generated pre-push hook carries exactly one gate, `cargo fmt --all --check`, and no reference to the sweep, so the cheapest and best-located check in the tree runs only when somebody remembers it -- and under the standing ruling that is where it stays. ",

    "WHAT IS NOW HARDER TO DO THAN BEFORE: NOTHING. This is a RECORD and not a REPAIR; the class stands at mitigatable for this specimen and no reader may cite it as coverage -- see [[a_written_row_is_not_a_firing_mechanism]]. THE ONE PRACTICE THAT DID FIRE, offered as the interim and not as the mechanism: run the REQUIRED LANE'S OWN INSTRUMENT locally -- `claim_executor --required-ci --required-lane witnesses` -- which carries the parse sweep as its FIRST PHASE and exits zero on the repaired tree. The discrimination is established across two heads with one instrument at no runner cost. THE CHEAPER ROUTE IS THE SAME WALK: the standalone `v1_src_dag_parse` bin and that phase both call `run_dag_parse_sweep` over the shared `DAG_PARSE_SWEEP_ROOTS` roster, so they cover the same files -- and the sweep alone answers in seconds where the composed lane takes minutes. ",
  ],

